d3d12: Stage CPU-written buffers in write-back memory under WSL2

Buffers the CPU writes, texture upload staging among them, went in
D3D12_HEAP_TYPE_UPLOAD, write-combined memory. WSL2's GPU
paravirtualization maps that memory uncached, on an integrated GPU and a
discrete one alike: writing it ran at 383 MB/s against 13049 MB/s for
write-back memory on a Radeon 780M, so a 1080p glTexSubImage2D took 25 ms
and a video's frames kept a core three quarters busy. This first covered
UMA devices only; a discrete GPU's upload heap is system memory too, and
Dozen already gives its host-visible memory write-back pages on every
adapter (dzn-wsl-write-back).

Give them a custom heap with write-back CPU pages in L0, as readback
buffers have, when not building for Windows.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_bufmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_bufmgr.cpp
@@ -144,6 +144,20 @@ d3d12_bo_new(struct d3d12_screen *screen, uint64_t size, const pb_desc *pb_desc)
       d3d12_evicted : d3d12_resident;
 
    D3D12_HEAP_PROPERTIES heap_pris = GetCustomHeapProperties(dev, heap_type);
+   /* CPU-written buffers, texture upload staging among them, live in
+    * write-back memory, as readback ones do and as Dozen's host-visible
+    * memory types do. WSL2's GPU paravirtualization maps write-combined
+    * memory uncached, on an integrated GPU and a discrete one alike:
+    * writing it ran 34 times slower on a Radeon 780M (383 against 13049
+    * MB/s), and a 1080p glTexSubImage2D took 25 ms.
+    */
+#ifndef _WIN32
+   if (heap_type == D3D12_HEAP_TYPE_UPLOAD) {
+      heap_pris.Type = D3D12_HEAP_TYPE_CUSTOM;
+      heap_pris.CPUPageProperty = D3D12_CPU_PAGE_PROPERTY_WRITE_BACK;
+      heap_pris.MemoryPoolPreference = D3D12_MEMORY_POOL_L0;
+   }
+#endif
    HRESULT hres = dev->CreateCommittedResource(&heap_pris,
                                               heap_flags,
                                               &res_desc,
